// Part III — Reference. Declared mode: reference.
page ref_mod_service {
  sites = [:manual]
  title = "service module (Windows)"

  chapter_header "service module (Windows)" {
    kicker       = "Reference · reference"
    reading_time = "2 min read"
    updated      = "2026-10-19"
    version      = "config-weave 0.1.0"
  }

  p <<'PROSE'
`use service` manages Windows services through the Service Control Manager.
It is Windows-only in this version: manage Linux services by running
`systemctl` through the [shell module](ref_mod_shell). The module is
registered on every platform so a playbook compiles and validates
identically everywhere; on Linux and macOS every call returns a runtime
error. Every function takes the service name and returns
`Result[…, string]`.
PROSE

  h2 "status"

  code rust {
    source = <<'SRC'
service::status(name: string) -> Result[string, string]
SRC
  }

  p "The current state of a service: `running`, `stopped`, `start_pending`, `stop_pending`, `paused`, `pause_pending` or `continue_pending`. A state the module does not recognise is reported as `unknown`."

  h2 "start, stop and restart"

  code rust {
    source = <<'SRC'
service::start(name: string) -> Result[unit, string]
service::stop(name: string) -> Result[unit, string]
service::restart(name: string, opts: Value) -> Result[unit, string]
service::start_with(name: string, opts: Value) -> Result[unit, string]
service::stop_with(name: string, opts: Value) -> Result[unit, string]
SRC
  }

  p "Starts, stops or restarts a service and returns once it has reached the target state, so a re-check straight after apply sees `running` or `stopped`, never a `*_pending` state. Each first waits out any pending state. `start` on a `paused` service continues it. `start` on a running service and `stop` on a stopped one are no-ops. `restart` stops the service, waits, starts it and waits again."

  p "The wait polls the service at a tenth of the wait hint it reports, between 100 ms and 1 s, for up to 60 seconds. `restart` and the `_with` forms take an options map with the key `timeout` (seconds, int or float; in `restart` it applies to each phase); `Value::Null` keeps the defaults. On timeout the call returns an `Err` naming the last state it saw. If the service drops back to its starting state after going pending (for example it crashes while starting), the call fails at once."

  p "`stop_with` and `restart` also take `stop_dependents` (bool, default `false`). When it is `true`, the call first stops every dependent service that is not already stopped, in the order the SCM lists them (the reverse of start order, so a dependent of a dependent stops first), each with the same timeout and wait. It then stops the service. `restart` starts the service again and then starts the dependents it stopped, in reverse stop order. A dependent that was already stopped stays stopped. A dependent that fails to stop or start ends the call with an `Err` naming it. `start_with` does not take `stop_dependents`; passing it is an `Err`."

  h2 "dependents"

  code rust {
    source = <<'SRC'
service::dependents(name: string) -> Result[List[string], string]
SRC
  }

  p "The names of the services that depend on `name`, directly or through another dependent, in any state, sorted. An empty list means nothing depends on it."

  h2 "set_startup and startup"

  code rust {
    source = <<'SRC'
service::set_startup(name: string, mode: string) -> Result[unit, string]
service::startup(name: string) -> Result[string, string]
SRC
  }

  p "`set_startup` sets the startup type to `automatic`, `automatic_delayed`, `manual` or `disabled`. `automatic_delayed` is Automatic (Delayed Start); setting plain `automatic` clears the delayed flag. `startup` reads the type back as one of those four, or `boot` or `system` for driver start types, or `other` for anything else."

  code rust {
    source = <<'SRC'
use service
use value

fn apply(props: Value) -> Result[ApplyResult, string] {
    service::set_startup("Spooler", "disabled")?
    service::stop("Spooler")?
    Ok(ApplyResult::Success)
}
SRC
  }
}
